### Granting access to QuickSuite Resources

[Example issue](https://mojdt.slack.com/archives/C4PF7QAJZ/p1767967315270389)
A user may ask to be granted to certain QuickSuite resources. This could be because they've taken ownership of a project but not been transferred ownership.

- Go to QuickSuite in the compute production account using a profile that can manage assets.
- Go to Manage QuickSuite in the top right corner of the UI.
- Go to Manage assets
- Here you can search for assets (Dashboards, analyses, data sets and data sources) via name and click the 3 dots to share with a user via their Justice email
- If the user doesn't have the name for the asset they want access to, you may be able to infer it via API calls to QuickSight
    - [describe dashboard](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quicksight/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeDashboard.html) will allow you to see a list of dataset arns
    - [describe data set](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quicksight/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeDataSet.html) will allow you to see the data source arn linked to it (but is unreliable for the data source name)
    - [describe data source](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quicksight/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeDataSource.html) will give you the data source name
        - As per the example issue, you will need to make a call to describe data set to get the ID of the data source, then call describe data source to get the name of the source to share it with an individual. You can get the ID of the data set from the manage assets page in QuickSuite if the user has the name of the data set.
        - `aws quicksight describe-data-set --aws-account-id <acc_id> --data-set-id <set_id>`
        - `aws quicksight describe-data-source --aws-account-id <acc_id> --data-source-id <source_id>`

### UV sync and clear cache to enable .trivyignore file to be applied

[Support query link](https://mojdt.slack.com/archives/C4PF7QAJZ/p1768907607347569) and [solution link](https://mojdt.slack.com/archives/C4PF7QAJZ/p1768909568126659?thread_ts=1768907607.347569&cid=C4PF7QAJZ)

This issue occurs when an analytical-platform-airflow-base-python user added a CVE to their trivyignore file, but it was not picked up by subsequent runs of the scan-container workflow (which uses the [shared-scan-container workflow](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/analytical-platform-airflow-github-actions/blob/main/.github/workflows/shared-scan-container.yml)). They were also using uv and had a uv.lock file.

### CaDeT deployed tables visible in Athena but not in QuickSight

These two workflows must complete successfully for the user to view new CaDeT tables in QuickSight:

[post-deploy-register-table-apc (event-type: metadata-to-apc)](https://github.com/moj-analytical-services/create-a-derived-table/actions/workflows/post-deploy-register-table-apc.yaml), in create-a-derived-table, which uses the metadata from CaDeT Deploys to announce the existence of Databases and Tables to analytical-platform-compute-production AWS account. This is triggered in the final step of a deploy workflow job.

[Terraform Plan and Apply (data-engineering-database-access)](https://github.com/moj-analytical-services/data-engineering-database-access/actions/workflows/terraform-deploy.yaml), which constantly gets state locked, which applies the individual user permissions required to access data. Follow these instructions to remove the state lock:

1. Clone `https://github.com/moj-analytical-services/data-engineering-database-access`
2. Boot dev container.
3. `cd terraform/analytical-platform-compute-production/01-permissions-configuration`
4. `aws-sso login`
5. `aws-sso exec --profile analytical-platform-management-production:AdministratorAccess`
6. `terraform init`
7. `terraform plan` << This will fail and give you the lock ID
8. `terraform force-unlock -force ${LOCK_ID}`


### Creating a new Webapp via Control Panel

[Example issue](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/data-platform-support/issues/1537)

A user may request for a new Webapp to be created. We need to register it in Control Panel to allow access to data.

- Go to the [webapps page in Control Panel](https://controlpanel.services.analytical-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/webapps/).
- Click the Register an app button (If you can't see this, you will need to be added as a superuser. Contact a dev)
- In the form, you will need to refer to the support template and add to the appropriate fields
    - Paste the github link under "Where is your app located?" into "GitHub repository URL"
    - Paste the cloud platform namespace under "What is your cloud platform namespace?" into "Cloud platform namespace" without any environment suffix (e.g data-platform-app-opg-ci-dashboard without the -dev or -prod)
    - If they have specified a bucket under "Which data warehouse (s3 bucket) does your app need access to", select the "connect an existing webapp data source" radio button and select the appropriate bucket using the dropdown.
    - Leave the "Access via Cloud Platform" box unticked.
    - Click the register app button
- Once the app has been created, click on the app name to go to the management page.
    - Scroll down to the App Admins section and add their user as an admin
    - Revoke your own admin status
- Notify the user that the app has been created in control panel and provide them with [guidance on managing the application](https://user-guidance.analytical-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/apps/static-app.html#manage-the-application)

### VSCode failing to start

[Example issue](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/data-platform-support/issues/1624)

A user's VSCode may fail to start with an error like - Error serving request: An error was encountered downloading the server, please retry: No such file or directory (os error 2)

- Access EFS in the prod cluster - `kubectl exec -i -t -n default efs-app -c app "--" sh`
- Navigate to their VSCode folder - `cd /data/<user>/vscode/`
- Inside here, delete the .vscode and .vscode-server folders (the "." is important!)
    - `rm -rf .vscode`
    - `rm -rf .vscode-server`
- Delete the user's VSCode deployment - `kubectl -n <namespace> delete deployment <deployment-name>`
- Go to control panel admin page
    - Go to tool deployments
    - Find the user's active vscode deployment and untick the active flag
- Ask the user to refresh the tools page and redeploy their VSCode

### Export Users CSV from Control Panel

[Example issue](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/data-platform-support/issues/1702)

From time to time, teams get in touch asking for a mapping of AP users GitHub names to their Justice email address. The issue above is an example of the request. We have previously agreed this team can have this information, this is how to provide it:

1. [Access the Control Panel Admin](https://controlpanel.services.analytical-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/admin/) using the link or via the main navigation in Control Panel. You need to be a superuser to be access the admin. If you are not one, ask another superuser to make you one.
2. Select "Users" from the [list of links under the API heading](https://controlpanel.services.analytical-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/admin/api/user/).
3. Use the checkbox to select all users (or a subset if required).

    Note: when selecting all users, you must select the top checkbox, then also the "Select all xxxx users" link.

4. Under the "Actions" dropdown, select "Export selected users as CSV" then click "Go". This will trigger a download in your browser.
5. Open the downloaded file on your machine, and remove any columns that are not needed. In the past, I have included only "username", "alpha_role_arn", "justice_email" and "date_joined".

    Note: Be sure to include the "justice_email" column, not the "email" column, as the "email" column can contain personal email addresses.

6. Export the modified file to a CSV, and then send it to them direct via slack - do not upload the CSV to the GitHub support ticket.
7. Close any related GitHub issue.
